{
  "reason": "The historical GRURec experiment improved macro validation HR@10 from 0.505 to 0.5275, supporting retention of its recurrent architecture and training setup. Electronics declined from 0.420 to 0.410, motivating a controlled objective experiment without establishing that the loss caused the decline. Modify model_design only: sampled cross-entropy tests direct competition against the negative pool while preserving the successful model and evaluation pipeline.",
  "module": [
    "model_design"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Replace only the BPR-max objective and its 0.001 negative-score penalty inside ranking_loss(model, seq, target) with sampled softmax cross-entropy, preserving the function signature and existing variable names. Retain encoded features, selected rows and columns, positives, 256 shared uniform negatives, dot-product-plus-learned-bias scores, seen-item masking, and the MAX_POSITIONS=2048 cap; this isolates whether direct candidate competition improves the historical GRURec result. After the existing usable-row filtering and float32 casts, mask invalid negative_scores with negative infinity, concatenate positive_scores[:, None] as column zero with the masked negative_scores, and apply mean torch.nn.functional.cross_entropy against device-local long zero labels, retaining the differentiable zero-loss fallback when no usable rows remain. Keep temperature at one, introduce no additional penalty or sampling correction, and preserve GRURec, its two 128-dimensional recurrent layers, tied embeddings, item bias, dropout, 64-item default history, random-prefix augmentation, AdamW settings, scheduler, clipping, environment-controlled 200-epoch default, validation cadence, and single-best-checkpoint selection. Preserve preprocessing seed 0, training and evaluation seeds 42, supplied splits, all four category routes, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, single-GPU execution within the shared budget, and the existing predictor writer and prediction signatures loading exactly one freshly trained checkpoint per category; judge the hypothesis through pinned host macro HR@10 on 200 validation users per category with 99 unique negatives, without hidden-test access or assuming gains.",
    "training_evaluation": null
  }
}
